@      *$SET TRACE ASMLIST COPYLIST PARAS REF 
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.                                         
       PROGRAM-ID.   MPTZ013.                                           
       AUTHOR.       PENNY GENOVESE.                                    
       DATE-WRITTEN. NOVEMBER 01, 1993.                                 
      ***************************************************************** 
      *SYSTEM NAME:   EDITORIAL SYSTEMS                                 
      *APPL NAME:     OEM PARTS UPDATE                                  
      *PROGRAM NAME:  MPTZ013 - SUPERSESSION REVERSAL PROGRAM           
      *LANGUAGE:      COBOL II / Oracle                                 
      *                                                                 
      *DESCRIPTION:                                                     
      *  FUNCTION: THIS PGM IS SIMILIAR TO THE SUPERSESSION PGM USED IN 
      *            THE PARTS UPDATE SYSTEM (MPTZ024) EXCEPT FOR:        
      *            1) THE TRANSACTION TYPE PROCESED IS "R"              
      *            2) THE OLD PART, NEW PART, AND EFF DATE IN THE TRANS 
      *               MUST MATCH AN EXISTING SUPERSESSION REC.          
      *               (TRANS OLD = PART-NUMBER, 
      *                TRANS NEW = SUPERSEDING-PART-NUMBER, AND
      *                TRANS EFF DT = SUPR-EFF-DT OF SUPERSESSION.)      
      *            3) THE PROGRAM REVERSES THE EXISTING SUPERSESSION    
      *               BY CHANGING ALL LINES ASSOCIATED TO THE "NEW"     
      *               PART TO POINT TO THE "OLD" PART; THEREFORE WHEN   
      *               COMPLETED, ALL ASSOCIATIONS WILL POINT TO "OLD"   
      *               PART # AND "NEW" PART FOR THIS PART SUPPLIER/COUNTRY 
      *               WILL NOT EXIST
      *            4) THE REVERSAL TRANSACTION IS NOT POSTED IN THE     
      *               ORACLE SUPERSESSION TABLE.                        
      *            5) THE EXISTING Oracle SUPERSESSION (THAT IT MATCHED 
      *               on) IS ALSO DELETED.                              
      *                                                                 
      *            NOTE - REVERSE TRANSACTION MUST BE SORTED BY EFF. DAT
      *                   IN DESCENDING ORDER (SO THAT LAST ONE IN GETS 
      *                   REVERSED FIRST).                              
      *                                                                 
      *  INPUT:    CONTROL INFORMATION (PROGRAM PARM FILE)              
      *            REFORMATTED TRANSACTION FILE                         
      *                                                                 
      *  I/O:      Oracle PART_SUPPLIER TABLE
      *            Oracle PART_SUPPLIER_COUNTRY TABLE
      *            Oracle SERVICE_CATEGORY_DETAIL TABLE
      *            Oracle DETAIL_PART_XREF TABLE
      *            Oracle PART_ALTPART_XREF TABLE
      *            Oracle ACQ_BATCH_REPORTS TABLE
      *            Oracle ACQ_BATCH_RESTART TABLE
      *                                                                 
      *  OUTPUT:   DATABASE UPDATE CONTROL REPORT                       
      *                                                                 
      * SIGNIFICANT PROCESSING NARRATIVE:                               
      *   PROGRAM USES A CONTROL FILE TO DETERMINE WHICH OEM IS BEING   
      *   PROCESSED. (THIS IS THE SAME PARM USED BY ALL OEM UPDT PGMS)  
      *                                                                 
      *   1) VALIDATES CONTROL FILE PARAMETERS.                         
      *   2) CHECK IF RESTART ROW FOUND INDICATING RESTART RUN          
      *   3) READS TRANS RECORD AND VALIDATES THAT SUPERSESSION IS      
      *      IN Oracle TABLE. (NOTE - TRANS MUST MATCH EXACTLY TO     
      *      existing SUPERSESSION)                                     
      *   4) IF VALID TRANSACTION, SUPERSESSION IS PERFORMED.           
      *      A) OLD PART IS INSERTED                                    
      *      B) ALL LINES ASSOCIATED TO NEW PART ARE CHANGED TO OLD     
      *      C) NEW PART ROW IS DELETED                                 
      *      D) EXISTING SUPERSESSION ROW IS DELETED                    
      *   5) AT END OF RUN, CONTROL REPORT IS PRODUCED SHOWING Oracle   
      *      table ACTIVITY AND TRANSACTION ACTIVITY                    
      *                                                                 
      *   *  COMMITS PERFORMED EVERY 5000 ROWS (LIMIT IS SET IN WRK STG)
      *   *  RESTART ROW WRITTEN AT EACH COMMIT POINT. (AT SUCCESSFUL   
      *         END, IT IS DELETED.))                                   
      *                                                                 
      * CALLED PROGRAMS:                                                
      *            ILBOABNO - ABEND ROUTINE                             
           CALL "dberrmsg" USING SQLCA ERROR-MESSAGE ERROR-LENGTH.
      *                                                                 
      * CONTROL CARD:                                                   
      *  (SAME CONTROL CARD THAT'S USED IN THE UPDATE PROGRAMS)         
      *                                                                 
      *  OEM=XXX,REGN=X,EFFDT=XX/XX/XXXX,REPLACE=X,RUNTYP=XXX,          
      *       1       2           3              4         5            
      *                                                                 
      *  NAGSTYP=XXXXXXXX                                               
      *             6                                                   
      *                                                                 
      *       1 - NUMERIC; PART SUPPLIER NUMBER WHICH YOU ARE PROCESSING 
      *                                                                 
      *       2 - ALPHA; PART SUPPLIER COUNTRY OF THE OEM (U = US, C = CAN)
      *                                                                 
      *       3 - NUMERIC; PRICE EFFECTIVE DATE AS SPECIFIED BY THE
      *           OEM  (FORMAT MM/DD/YYYY; MUST BE GREATER THAN LAST RUN
      *           UNLESS THIS IS REPLACEMENT RUN - THEN MUST = LAST RUN)
      *                                                                 
      *       4 - ALPHA; REPLACEMENT INDICATOR (FOR PRICE UPDATE PGM);  
      *           (N = NEW RUN, PRICES WILL BE UPDATED - CURRENT MOVED  
      *           TO PREVIOUS THEN TRANSACTION PRICE MOVED TO CURRENT;  
      *           Y = REPLACEMENT RUN, TRANSACTION PRICE MOVED DIRECTLY 
      *           OVER CURRENT PRICE; USED FOR CORRECTING MISPRICING.)  
      *                                                                 
      *       5 - ALPHA; TYPE OF RUN (OEM = OEM, SUP = SUPPLIMENTAL)    
      *           (USED BY REPORT PROGRAM MPTZ007)                      
      *                                                                 
      *       6 - ALPHA; TYPE OF NAGS RUN (FOR NAGS RUN, EITHER "IMPORT"
      *           OR "DOMESTIC"; ANY OTHER RUNS, "N/A")                 
      *           (PRINTED IN HEADING - JUST TO DISTINGUISH BETWEEN THE 
      *            IMPORT AND DOMESTIC RUN REPORTS)                     
      *                                                                 
      * MODIFICATION LOG:                                               
      * --DATE-- -BY- ------DESCRIPTION---------------------------------
      * 01/23/2019  BY:   PENNY GENOVESE
      *             DESC: No code change. Added mod note so pgm could be
      *                   recompiled with new version of mptb002.cpy.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 05/17/2014  BY:   PENNY GENOVESE
      *             DESC: NO CODE CHANGES MADE. ADDED MOD NOTE SO THAT 
      *                   PROGRAM COULD BE RECOMPILED FOR ORACLE 11G /
      *                   IBM 770 MIGRATION.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 02/07/03 BY:   PENNY GENOVESE
      *          DESC: ADDED LOGIC TO HANDLE SCENARIO WHERE OLD PART
      *                ALREADY EXISTS. (OCCURS WHEN THERE'S A LOOPING
      *                SUPER IN THE DATABASE.)                          
      *           
      * 01/03/02 BY:   GAIL WALDER
      *          DESC: MODIFIED DUE TO NEW SUPERSESSION LOGIC:
      *                CHECK FOR DUPLICATE 'PARTS-TO-BE-REVERSED'
      *                (TR-NEW-PART-NUM).
      *                PROCESS THE FIRST INSTANCE IN A SERIES OF DUPLICATES,
      *                BYPASS REVERSING THE REST OF THE DUPLICATES. 
      *                THE FIRST TRANSACTION'S TR-OLD-PART-NUM BECOMES 
      *                THE SUPERSEDING PART.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 02/19/01 BY:   GAIL WALDER
      *          DESC: 1. MODIFIED FOR CORRECTION DETAIL_PART_XREF COUNTS
      *                   WHEN UPDATING OLD PART WITH SUPERSESSION PART DATA
      *                2. ADDED ALTERNATE PART IMPACT COUNTS WHEN UPDATING
      *                   OLD PART WITH SUPERSESSION PART DATA
      * --------------------------------------------------------------------
      * 02/14/01  BY: MARINA BOGOPOLSKY
      *           DESC: ADDED Y1500-SQL-PROCEDURE-ERROR PARAGRAPH
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 08/24/00 BY:   GAIL WALDER
      *          DESC: RACE II REVISIONS:
      *                1. CONVERTED FOR NEW ERD STRUCTURE AND 
      *                   PART TABLE DEFAULTS
      *                2. ADDED INITIALIZE FOR RETURNED VARIABLES
      *                   IN SELECT PROCEDURE CALLS
      * --------------------------------------------------------------------
      * 08/24/00 BY:   GAIL WALDER
      *          DESC: RACE II REVISIONS:
      *                1. CONVERTED FOR NEW DATABASE STRUCTURE
      *                2. CONVERTED EMBEDDED SQL TO PACKAGE/PROCEDURE CALLS
